rows=[
(1,'KEEP',[I,II],'theory','Swing pumping by a specified phase-dependent change of body height','Newton pendulum energy/torque and changing effective length/inertia describe the given crouching/standing cycle. Parametric growth and phase stability are ordinary oscillations; exact body geometry can be a declared model.'),
(2,'KEEP',[I],'numerical','Air-drag projectile flight inferred from a given vertical return time','Bullet size/material and 12.5-second return time support a declared ordinary empirical drag model, numerical Newton integration and range-angle optimization. A drag coefficient/air state is needed for numbers, but deriving a specialized viscous-flow law is not expressly requested.'),
(3,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Nonuniform rod and unilateral wall contact during a fall','Rigid-body force/torque, inertia and vanishing wall reaction are ordinary mechanics. Parameterize mass distribution and verify the stated floor-pivot geometry; an overconstrained literal contact can imply immediate detachment rather than a fabricated sliding-ladder solution.'),
(4,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Recoil of a carriage carrying an explicitly inviscid draining L-tube','Given dimensions, equivalent carriage mass, negligible viscosity/tension and noninterfering outflow define an ordinary plug-flow/pressure and momentum-energy model. Coupled carriage/liquid Newton equations determine the symmetric-case terminal speed.'),
(5,'KEEP',[I,VI],'theory','Classical charge trajectory from the symmetry plane of a fixed dipole','Classical mechanics and electrostatics are explicitly stipulated. Coulomb dipole potential, force, conserved energy and orbit integration determine turning point and time; no quantum scattering is needed.'),
(6,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Prescribed kinetic-energy constraint and elastic bouncing on a small slope','The drag ansatz and constant-speed requirement determine alpha from Newton work balance. It may have negative sign, explaining the artificial active force. Differential motion and bounce-map stability are mathematics of this supplied Newton model.'),
(7,'REJECT',[],'theory','Trajectories from a nonstandard square-root Hamiltonian','The formal H is supplied, but its canonical equations and momentum/velocity interpretation are not. Those central outside analytical-mechanics postulates define the entire trajectory task; it is not an ordinary p-squared kinetic plus Newton spring energy.'),
(8,'BORDERLINE',[I,II],'experimental','Inferring an elastic parameter from electrical collision-contact timing','Axial longitudinal wave travel in aligned long prisms would infer a scalar modulus using ordinary Hooke/waves. General hung prism contact can instead require an unsupplied three-dimensional contact compliance law. Dimensions/orientation/contact idealization are absent, leaving the required elastic method uncertain.'),
(9,'KEEP',[I],'numerical','Earth angular-momentum response to changing traffic lane direction','Rigid-body angular momentum and the offset between opposite traffic lanes determine the small effect under declared traffic geography/speed/population estimates. No special geophysics theory is required.'),
(10,'KEEP',[I],'numerical','Estimating tidal lunar recession from angular-momentum transfer','Newton orbit energy/angular momentum and Earth spin loss relate tidal torque to lunar recession. An empirical lag/torque or day-length trend must be declared for a numerical estimate; the task need not derive a microscopic ocean/Earth constitutive response.'),
(11,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Rotating-liquid free surface in a cylindrical cup','For the declared steady co-rotating idealization, centrifugal acceleration and hydrostatic pressure yield a paraboloid. Actual stirrer angular speed need not equal bulk-fluid speed; an exact viscous mixer flow is an additional unrequested model.'),
(12,'REJECT',[],'theory','Viscous-vortex Navier-Stokes solutions and interacting vortex centres','Only the name of Navier-Stokes and an initial vorticity are supplied. The viscous constitutive/evolution equation, vorticity transport and singular point-vortex velocity law are central specialized fluid prerequisites, not merely solving a fully provided PDE.'),
(13,'KEEP',[I,VII],'theory','Mutual torques and total rotation of two T-arranged magnetic dipoles','Actual dipole/ruler drawing fixes perpendicular orientations. Standard dipole field and torque plus force moments and total angular momentum resolve unequal local torques and the hung-ruler outcome.'),
(14,'KEEP',[VI],'experimental','Resistance measurement without breaking a resistor network','Ohm/Kirchhoff response, independent test excitations and node-voltage/current observations determine measurable resistances or identify nonidentifiability. Accessible nodes/parallel equivalent branches must be specified; ordinary circuit inverse measurement is the task.'),
(15,'KEEP',[VI],'theory','Accessible voltage and energy of two hidden oppositely charged capacitors','Electrostatic capacitance, conserved charge on the inaccessible middle conductor and external-port energy accounting determine observable voltage and extractable energy. Zero-point is a quoted analogy, not quantum zero-point dynamics.'),
(16,'KEEP',[I,VI,VII,IX],'theory','Field angular momentum and apparent inertia of a rotating charged insulating rod','Gauss/Ampere fields, standard electromagnetic momentum density and its spatial angular integral compare mechanical and field contributions. Negative-inertia interpretation is checked by ordinary field energy/angular momentum, without microscopic or quantum material theory.'),
(17,'KEEP',[VI],'theory','Square resistor-grid separation asymptotics and one missing edge','The complete graph/resistance and neighbouring calibration are provided. Kirchhoff discrete Green functions and a finite edge-removal correction give arbitrary-pair resistance; lattice integral asymptotics are mathematical work.'),
(18,'KEEP',[I,III,IV],'theory','Heavy-piston adiabatic expansion and staged/frictional entropy accounting','All four parts use ideal-gas adiabatic energy, external-pressure work, piston kinetic energy and entropy including final environmental heat. Friction path details must be accounted for; no outside thermodynamic model is central.'),
(19,'REJECT',[],'theory','Motion and possible reversal of a thermally lagged disk in background radiation','Blackness and small velocity specify thermal absorption qualitatively, but the moving-frame angular radiation intensity and emitted momentum transformation are not supplied. Those central first-order relativistic radiative-drag relations are needed for the requested v(t) and reversal criterion; a qualitative photon-recoil critique alone does not complete this task.'),
(20,'KEEP',[I],'experimental','Coin-drop outcome statistics and experimental sensitivity growth','Rigid-body fall/impact, phase-space initial conditions and fitted sensitivity rates are ordinary mechanics/data analysis. The asserted increasing fairness or positive Lyapunov exponent is not a guaranteed fact; an integrable free-flight model can expose that limitation without outside physics.'),
(21,'KEEP',[],'data_analysis','Random-walk price and supplied asynchronous broker transaction rules','All sell/rest/buy timing rules and zero transaction costs are printed. Probability, renewal timing and order statistics determine profit distributions once random-walk/timing and broker-count parameters are declared. This is a mathematical toy model, not financial advice.'),
(22,'KEEP',[IV],'data_analysis','Trap ageing under completely supplied waiting-time and reset laws','Exponential trap lifetime, heavy-tail lifetime distribution, uniform resets and Gibbs-Boltzmann equilibrium relation are all supplied. Probability flow gives a master equation, equilibrium lifetime weights and renewal survival/ageing calculations; no molecular dynamics must be supplied.'),
(23,'KEEP',[II],'theory','Higher asymptotic terms of a fully supplied scattering wave equation','The exact stationary PDE, incident/outgoing leading form and rapid-decay conditions are provided. Green-integral/asymptotic expansion and finite-radius/angular wave interpretation use mathematics and ordinary waves; no quantum probability law is needed to derive the requested series.'),
(24,'REJECT',[],'theory','Accelerating Airy quantum packet and transformations under a linear potential','Airy integral and trial wavefunction/coordinate ansatz are supplied, but the time-dependent Schrodinger differential equation is only named, not written. That central outside quantum evolution law and physical packet interpretation are needed for all coefficients and potential/accelerated-frame results.'),
(25,'REJECT',[],'theory','Curved-space Kepler mechanics followed by quantum spectrum','Sphere/projective coordinates and potential are supplied, but canonical/Poisson dynamical postulates and curved-space quantization/operator prescription are not. Those central specialized mechanics/quantum prerequisites control the conserved-algebra and spectrum task.'),
(26,'REJECT',[],'theory','Quantum states and tunnelling of a multi-cover pendulum','The classical configuration is described, but quantum evolution, low-state tunnelling/splitting and symmetry representation rules are not supplied. They dominate the requested comparison.'),
(27,'KEEP',[II],'theory','Finite-grid angular differential operators and their spectra','A second-derivative stencil and cubic lattice are supplied. Coordinate chain rules define angular derivatives; finite-difference matrices, eigenvalues/eigenvectors and commutators are ordinary mathematics. The additional spin analogy is peripheral; no central quantum state calculation is required.'),
(28,'REJECT',[],'theory','Second-quantized diatomic electron model','Hamiltonian terms and orbital labels are supplied, but Fock-state construction, fermion anticommutation/occupation/spin rules and physical state interpretation are not. Those missing quantum prerequisites dominate every block, ground-state and chemistry result.'),
(29,'REJECT',[],'theory','Excited atom crossing a resonant Fabry-Perot cavity','No atom-field dipole Hamiltonian/coupling, semiclassical internal-state evolution or final joint-state prescription is supplied. Those specialized quantum-optical relations are central despite familiar interferometer context.'),
(30,'REJECT',[],'theory','Two-spin measuring map, interaction Hamiltonian and density matrix','The input-output state map is genuinely given. Its conversion into a physical generator, spin operators, density matrix and reversibility still requires unsupplied quantum time-evolution/state postulates; the map alone is not a complete operational quantum model.'),
(31,'REJECT',[],'theory','Magnetic gap of an armchair nanotube in a named tight-binding model','Geometry is supplied, but tight-binding hopping/dispersion, magnetic phase coupling, electronic boundary states and Fermi occupation are not. Those specialized condensed-matter prerequisites centrally determine the gap/transition.'),
(32,'REJECT',[],'theory','Quantum effective dynamics with infinitely many oscillator dimensions','Frequency scaling and qualitative perturbation are given, but quantum oscillator state/perturbative elimination and effective-dynamics prescriptions are not. Central quantum/field-like machinery is unsupplied.'),
(33,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Transit-time penalty for an approximate tunnel brachistochrone','Homogeneous Earth gravity is Newtonian and supplies the actual speed-radius relation. Variational time/path optimization and direct integration compare the true optimum with the constructed uniform-gravity cycloid family; difficult geometry is mathematics, not GR.'),
(34,'KEEP',[],'theory','Work-efficiency optimization under a fully supplied fatigue memory law','All performance, efficiency and exponential-memory definitions are printed. Differentiation yields a closed fatigue ODE; nonlinear evolution and variational/optimal-control mathematics answer constant-output and finite-work requests. No physiological model need be imported.')]
